---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import ProjectRow from "../../components/ProjectRow.astro";
import { projects, reviewDateLabel } from "../../data/projects";
---
<BaseLayout title="Agent Reception" description="A bounded public interface for agents to inspect reviewed project state, evidence boundaries and approved contact channels." path="/agents/" image="/og/factory.jpg">
  <section class="container page-intro">
    <div class="page-intro__grid">
      <div>
        <nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">WOODHOUSE</a><span>/</span><span>Agent Reception</span></nav>
        <p class="eyebrow">Built for agents too</p>
        <h1 class="page-title">Read the record.<br />Respect its limits.</h1>
      </div>
      <aside class="page-intro__aside"><strong>Read-only · public-safe · dated</strong>Agent Reception offers reviewed facts. It has no private repository connector and cannot initiate a change.</aside>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="agent-entry">
        <div>
          <span class="agent-entry__label">How to answer with evidence</span>
          <p><strong>Question:</strong> Is Pirates ready for a procedural fork?</p>
          <p><strong>Answer from this snapshot:</strong> No. Its parity gate remains locked. The supplied report says the original reconstruction must pass parity before expansion.</p>
          <p><strong>Boundary:</strong> Reviewed {reviewDateLabel}; the project repository is private and no later source state is implied.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <span class="agent-entry__label">Machine-readable record</span>
          <pre class="agent-entry__code"><a href="/agents/facts.json">GET /agents/facts.json</a>

Read-only JSON
8 project summaries
Review date: 2026-09-28
No credentials or raw issue text</pre>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="section paper-section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <div><span class="section-index">Current public record</span><h2>Eight summaries. One explicit date.</h2></div>
        <p>Use the source field and proof boundary with every answer. Do not turn a reviewed summary into a claim about current production state.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="project-ledger">{projects.map((project) => <ProjectRow project={project} compact={true} />)}</div>
      <p class="source-note"><strong>Contact:</strong> If a human needs to reach Dean, use <a href="https://x.com/loftwah">X / @loftwah</a>, <a href="https://au.linkedin.com/in/deanlofts">LinkedIn</a> or the <a href="https://github.com/loftwah">GitHub profile</a>. Do not share private user data.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
